{"result":"{
  "id": "19416",
  "key": "SFCC-855",
  "summary": "PWA installability: web app manifest, service worker, maskable icon, splash screen",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/19416",
  "description": "**Context**\n\nSurfaced by the SIT Gate's Lighthouse CI job (`lighthouserc.js`, `lighthouse:recommended` preset — in scope per this epic's \"CI/CD pipeline including... Lighthouse CI >90\"), running for the first time against a real deployed build (SIT bootstrap, 2026-09-01). The full preset is being kept as-is rather than narrowed, so these failing audits stay visible on every release branch's SIT Gate until built.\n\n**Failing audits (PWA installability group)**\n\n- `installable-manifest` — no web app manifest configured for install prompts\n- `service-worker` — no service worker registered (site isn't installable/offline-capable)\n- `maskable-icon` — manifest icons aren't maskable-safe for adaptive icon platforms\n- `splash-screen` — no splash screen configured for standalone/installed launch\n\n**Scope**\n\n- Add a web app manifest (`manifest.json`) with correct icons (including a maskable variant), theme colours, and start URL\n- Register a service worker (`worker/main.js` already exists as a Tier 1 file per `frozenFiles.md` — coordinate with Integration/SI Partner owner rather than editing directly)\n- Confirm splash-screen generation from the manifest config\n\n**Out of scope** (separate Lighthouse findings, not part of this story)\n\n- `csp-xss` — CSP hardening (unsafe-inline/unsafe-eval removal) is a separate, more involved security investigation\n- `unused-javascript`, `valid-source-maps`, `uses-rel-preconnect` — bundle/build hygiene, not installability",
