  "description": "**Context**\n\nSurfaced by the SIT Gate's Lighthouse CI job (`lighthouserc.js`, `lighthouse:recommended` preset — in scope per this epic's \"CI/CD pipeline including... Lighthouse CI >90\"), running for the first time against a real deployed build (SIT bootstrap, 2026-09-01).\n\nThe `content-security-policy` header **is** present and correctly built (`overrides/app/ssr/contentSecurityPolicy.ts`, wired via `helmet()` in `overrides/app/ssr.js`) — this is not a \"CSP missing\" bug. Lighthouse's `csp-xss` audit is failing because the policy currently relies on broad allowances rather than nonces/hashes:\n\n- `style-src` includes `'unsafe-inline'` — per the file's own comment, required by Chakra UI's runtime style injection (`useDefaults: true` replaces rather than merges a directive when given explicitly, so `'self'`/`'unsafe-inline'` are spelled out there deliberately)\n- `script-src` includes `'unsafe-eval'` (via MRT's own additions, not this file) plus a number of third-party wildcard origins (Stripe, PayPal, Adyen, Measmerize, Google Pay/Maps)\n\n**Why this isn't a quick fix**\n\nRemoving `'unsafe-inline'` without a nonce-based alternative would very likely break Chakra's styling across the whole app. Removing `'unsafe-eval'` risks breaking the already-integrated third-party payment/widget scripts. A real fix means:\n\n- Generating a per-request nonce and threading it through SSR rendering (Chakra's `<CacheProvider>`/emotion nonce support) and every inline `<script>`\n  - This touches `overrides/app/ssr.js`, which is on the **absolute never-touch list* in `AGENTS.md`/`frozenFiles.md` — no Tier-1-approver exception applies to that file. Any change there needs the Integration/SI Partner owner directly, not just Claude-assisted review\n- Verifying every third-party integration (payments, Measmerize, Google Maps/Pay) still functions under a tightened policy\n\n**Scope**\n\n- Design a nonce (or hash-based) CSP strategy compatible with Chakra UI's emotion-based styling\n- Thread the nonce through SSR rendering — requires the `ssr.js` owner (Integration/SI Partner)\n- Re-verify third-party script/style integrations under the tightened policy\n- Confirm `csp-xss` passes in `lighthouserc.js`'s `lighthouse:recommended` preset on the SIT Gate\n\n**Out of scope** (separate Lighthouse findings, not part of this story)\n\n- `installable-manifest`, `service-worker`, `maskable-icon`, `splash-screen` — see SFCC-855\n- `unused-javascript`, `valid-source-maps`, `uses-rel-preconnect` — bundle/build hygiene\n\n**Status:** logged as a known, accepted SIT Gate failure for now rather than fixed same-day — decided 2026-09-01 given the ssr.js constraint and the risk of breaking styling/payments without dedicated testing.",
